# Changelog required for new mod versions

Any release that bumps the mod version **must** include a matching changelog entry in the same change set.

## When this applies

- Bumping `<Version>` in `src/PeakShotgun/Peak.Shotgun.csproj`
- Any change intended as a new Thunderstore / mod release
- Do not bump `<Version>` unless a release was asked for (see `AGENTS.md`)

## Required updates (same change set)

1. `src/PeakShotgun/Peak.Shotgun.csproj` — new `<Version>`
2. `CHANGELOG.md` — new section for that exact version

`thunderstore.toml` copies `CHANGELOG.md` into the package; a missing or stale entry ships an empty/wrong changelog on Thunderstore.

## Changelog format

Newest version at the top. Match existing style:

```markdown
## X.Y.Z

- Short, player-facing bullet for each notable change
```

- Use the same version string as `<Version>` (e.g. `1.0.3`)
- Prefer concise, user-visible notes (fixes, features, config, behavior)
- Skip internal-only noise unless it affects players (e.g. CI-only bumps may still need a one-line note)

## Checklist before finishing a version bump

- [ ] `<Version>` bumped in the csproj
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` has a `## <that-version>` section with bullets
- [ ] Version strings match exactly
